IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part1`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part2`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part3`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part4`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part5`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part6`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part7`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part8`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part9`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part10`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-s5-definitions`
IMPORT `wa-seat`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for the Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) encoding.
-- Every expected value comes from ANSWERS.md, written from the source text before any .l4 file was opened.
-- The scenario number in each comment is the number in ANSWERS.md.  Nothing was edited to match the encoding without a record. Where triage afterwards changed an expected value, the `-- RECONCILED` comment above the assertion quotes the original and gives the reason.
-- Helpers (names start "ti") only build inputs or read a field out of a result; none re-implements a rule.

GIVETH A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
`ti no holidays` MEANS
    `Holidays that make an excluded day` WITH
        `public service holidays`              IS EMPTY
        `bank holidays in the relevant area`   IS EMPTY
        `public holidays in the relevant area` IS EMPTY

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF DATE
      bs IS A LIST OF DATE
      hs IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
`ti holidays` ps bs hs MEANS
    `Holidays that make an excluded day` WITH
        `public service holidays`              IS ps
        `bank holidays in the relevant area`   IS bs
        `public holidays in the relevant area` IS hs

GIVEN r IS A MAYBE `Reckoned period`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ti the last day by the calendar` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (x's `end`'s `last day by the calendar`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN r IS A MAYBE `Reckoned period`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ti the last day for doing the thing` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (x's `end`'s `last day for doing the thing`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN r IS A MAYBE `Reckoned period`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ti the first day of the period` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (x's `first day`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      u IS A `Unit of a period`
GIVETH A `Period of time`
`ti period of` n u MEANS `Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS n, `unit` IS u

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ti count of strings` xs MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN 1 PLUS `ti count of strings` rest

-- ===================== PART I: PRELIMINARY (ss 1-4) =====================

-- 2. s 2: the day this Act comes into operation is 1984-07-01
#ASSERT `the day this Act came into operation` EQUALS Date 1 7 1984
-- 3. s 2 with s 21: the moment is the beginning of 1984-07-01 (second 0)
#ASSERT `the moment a written law comes into operation` (Date 1 7 1984) EQUALS (`Moment of a day` WITH `the calendar day` IS Date 1 7 1984, `second of the day` IS 0)
-- 4. s 3(1): a written law of 1970, no carve-out: the Act applies
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `an Act` (Date 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 5. s 3(1)(a): express provision to the contrary: the Act does not apply
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `an Act` (Date 1 1 1970) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- 6. s 3(1)(b): an Act whose subject or context is inconsistent: the Act does not apply
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `an Act` (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- 7. s 3(1)(b),(c): subsidiary legislation, own context inconsistent, empowering Act's intent not: the Act applies
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `subsidiary legislation` (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 8. s 3(1)(c): subsidiary legislation, empowering Act's intent inconsistent: the Act does not apply
#ASSERT `this Act applies to the written law` `subsidiary legislation` (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- 9. s 3(2): this Act is treated as an Act passed after its own commencement (so s 17 applies to it)
#ASSERT `this Act is treated as an Act passed after its own commencement` EQUALS TRUE
-- 10. s 4: the Act binds the Crown
#ASSERT `the Crown is bound by this Act` EQUALS TRUE
-- 11. s 3(3): a 2024 Act that directly amends an existing law without repealing it entirely is not "passed after the commencement" for s 25
#ASSERT `counts as passed or made after the commencement for ss 17, 25, 43(6), 50 and 64` (Date 1 3 2024) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- 12. s 3(3): a 2024 Act that repeals a 1990 Act entirely is "passed after the commencement" for s 17
#ASSERT `counts as passed or made after the commencement for ss 17, 25, 43(6), 50 and 64` (Date 1 3 2024) FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- ===================== PART II: s 5 DEFINITIONS =====================

-- 13. s 5 "year": a year is a period of 12 months
#ASSERT `what the Act says a word for a length of time means` `the word year` EQUALS JUST `a period of 12 months`
-- 14a. s 5 "person" includes a public body
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "person" "a public body" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 14b. s 5 "person" includes a company
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "person" "a company" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 14c. s 5 "person" includes an unincorporated association (the Act's words: association or body of persons, corporate or unincorporate)
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "person" "an association or body of persons, corporate or unincorporate" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 15. s 5 "individual" means a natural person (the meaning of a "means" entry)
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "individual" "a natural person" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 16. s 5 "land" includes land covered with water
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "land" "land covered with water" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 17. s 5 "estate" includes a lien
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "estate" "lien" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 18a. s 5 "sign" includes a thumbprint
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sign" "thumbprint" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 18b. s 5 "sign" includes making a seal
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sign" "the affixing or making of a seal" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 19. s 5 "sign" and a typed name: not covered
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sign" "typing one's name" EQUALS NOTHING
-- 20a. s 5 "sell" includes barter
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sell" "barter" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 20b. s 5 "sell" includes expose for sale
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sell" "expose for sale" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 21. s 5 "sell" and a gift: not covered
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "sell" "gift" EQUALS NOTHING
-- 22. s 5 "swear" includes to affirm
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "swear" "to affirm" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 23. s 5 "will" includes a codicil
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "will" "a codicil" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 24a. s 5 "words" includes figures
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "words" "figures" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 24b. s 5 "words" includes symbols
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "words" "symbols" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 25. s 5 "writing" includes photocopying
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "writing" "photocopying" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 26a. s 5 "repeal" includes revoke
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "repeal" "revoke" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 26b. s 5 "repeal" includes delete
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "repeal" "delete" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 27. s 5 "repeal" and suspend: not covered
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "repeal" "suspend" EQUALS NOTHING
-- 28a. s 5 "power" includes a discretion
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "power" "discretion" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 28b. s 5 "function" includes jurisdictions
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "function" "jurisdictions" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 28c. s 5 "perform" includes the exercise of a power
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "perform" "the exercise of a power, responsibility, authority or jurisdiction" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 29. s 5 "financial year": the financial year ending 2025-06-30 begins on 2024-07-01
#ASSERT `the first day of the financial year ending in` 2025 EQUALS Date 1 7 2024
-- 30a. s 5 "court of summary jurisdiction": the Magistrates Court is one
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "court of summary jurisdiction" "the Magistrates Court" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 30b. s 5 "court of summary jurisdiction": the District Court is not one
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "court of summary jurisdiction" "the District Court" EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 31a. s 5 "judge": an auxiliary judge of the Supreme Court is a judge
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "judge" "an auxiliary judge of the Supreme Court" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 31b. s 5 "judge": a District Court judge is not a "judge"
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "judge" "a judge of the District Court" EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 32. s 5 "Governor": includes the officer for the time being administering the Government of the State
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "Governor" "the officer for the time being administering the Government of the State" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 33. s 5 "King" (Her Majesty ... Crown): includes the heirs and successors of the Sovereign
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "King" "the heirs and successors of the Sovereign" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 34. s 5 "Australia" means the Commonwealth of Australia (the meaning of a "means" entry)
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "Australia" "the Commonwealth of Australia" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 35a. s 5 "Australia Acts": the Commonwealth Act is one
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "Australia Acts" "the Australia Act 1986 of the Commonwealth" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 35b. s 5 "Australia Acts": the United Kingdom Act is one
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "Australia Acts" "the Australia Act 1986 of the United Kingdom" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 37. s 5 "enactment": a portion of a written law is an enactment
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "enactment" "any portion of a written law" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 38a. s 5 "written law": a repealed Act is not one
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "written law" "an Act that has been repealed" EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 38b. s 5 "written law": subsidiary legislation in force is one
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "written law" "all subsidiary legislation for the time being in force" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 39a. s 5 "subsidiary legislation": an order is
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "subsidiary legislation" "order" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 39b. s 5 "subsidiary legislation": a notice with no legislative effect is not
-- RECONCILED 39b: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "subsidiary legislation" "a notice without legislative effect" EQUALS JUST FALSE`; triaged against the text: genuine fork (reviewer's ambiguity): s 5 'subsidiary legislation' (l.241) 'made under any written law and having legislative effect' qualifies either only 'other instrument' (the encoding's reading, so the bare member 'notice' is subsidiary legislation) or the whole list (the reviewer's: a notice without legislative effect is not); the encoding answers NOTHING for the phrase 'a notice without legislative effect'. Registered as a fork in NOTES.md
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "subsidiary legislation" "a notice without legislative effect" EQUALS NOTHING
-- 41. s 5 "contravene": includes failing to comply with a requirement or condition
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "contravene" "a failure to comply with that requirement or condition" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 43a. s 5 "parent": includes an adoptive parent under the Adoption Act 1994
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "parent" "a person who is an adoptive parent under the Adoption Act 1994" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 43b. s 5 "parent" and a stepparent: not covered
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "parent" "a stepparent" EQUALS NOTHING
-- 45. s 5 "penalty": includes suspension or cancellation of a licence, registration or permit
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "penalty" "the suspension or cancellation of a licence, registration or permit" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 47. s 5 "Gazette": includes the electronic form
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "Gazette" "electronic form" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 51. s 5 "prescribed": prescribed by or under the written law in which the word occurs
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "prescribed" "prescribed by or under the written law in which the word occurs" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 52a. s 5 "under": includes pursuant to
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "under" "pursuant to" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 52b. s 5 "under": includes by virtue of
#ASSERT `the definition of the word lists the thing` "under" "by virtue of" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 55. s 5 "justice of the peace": "JP" is the same entry as "justice of the peace"
#ASSERT `the entry in section 5 for the word` "JP" EQUALS `the entry in section 5 for the word` "justice of the peace"

-- ===================== PART II: ss 6-19 =====================

-- 56a. s 6: a definition applies to the provision that contains it
#ASSERT `a definition or rule of interpretation applies to the provision` `it is a provision that contains the definition or rule` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 56b. s 6: a definition applies to other provisions of the same written law
#ASSERT `a definition or rule of interpretation applies to the provision` `it is another provision of the same written law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 57. s 7: an enactment partly in excess of the State's power is valid to the extent it is not in excess
#ASSERT `the extent of validity of an enactment` TRUE EQUALS `valid to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of the State`
-- 58. s 8: a present-tense provision applies to the circumstance as it arises
#ASSERT `a present tense provision applies to the circumstance as it arises` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 1990) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 59. s 9: other grammatical forms of a defined word have a corresponding meaning
#ASSERT `the word has a corresponding meaning` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 60a. s 10(a): "he" includes any individual of any gender
#ASSERT `a word indicating a person of a particular gender or sex includes` `an individual, of any gender or sex` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 60b. s 10(a): "he" includes a person that is not an individual
#ASSERT `a word indicating a person of a particular gender or sex includes` `a person that is not an individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 61a. s 10(c): a word in the singular includes the plural
#ASSERT elem `plural` (`the numbers a word in this number covers` `singular`) EQUALS TRUE
-- 61b. s 10(c): a word in the plural includes the singular
#ASSERT elem `singular` (`the numbers a word in this number covers` `plural`) EQUALS TRUE
-- 62. s 11: a reference to the Sovereign reigning at enactment or to the Crown is to the Sovereign for the time being
#ASSERT `the Sovereign meant by the reference` TRUE "the King" EQUALS JUST "the King"
-- 63. s 12(a): "the Minister" in an Act is the Minister administering the Act
#ASSERT `the Ministers a reference to the Minister covers` `an Act` "Minister A" NOTHING EQUALS LIST "Minister A"
-- 64. s 12(b): "the Minister" in subsidiary legislation is the Minister administering the Act under which it is made
#ASSERT `the Ministers a reference to the Minister covers` `subsidiary legislation` "Minister A" NOTHING EQUALS LIST "Minister A"
-- 65. s 12(c): "the Minister" includes a Minister acting for that Minister
#ASSERT elem "Minister B" (`the Ministers a reference to the Minister covers` `an Act` "Minister A" (JUST "Minister B")) EQUALS TRUE
-- 66. s 13(2): "British subject" in WA law is read as an Australian citizen
#ASSERT `a reference to a British subject is read as a reference to the person` `an Australian citizen` EQUALS TRUE
-- 67. s 13A(1): two persons living together marriagelike, not legally married to each other: a de facto relationship
#ASSERT `a de facto relationship exists between two persons` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 68. s 13A(1): two persons legally married to each other: not a de facto relationship
#ASSERT `a de facto relationship exists between two persons` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- 69. s 13A(3)(a): two persons of the same sex can be in a de facto relationship
#ASSERT `a de facto relationship exists between two persons` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 70. s 13A(3)(b): one is legally married to someone else: still a de facto relationship
#ASSERT `a de facto relationship exists between two persons` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- 73. s 13A(4): a person who has lived in a de facto relationship, where the context requires, is a de facto partner
#ASSERT `a person is a de facto partner` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- 74a. s 13B: a reference in a written law other than this Act to the Standards Association of Australia is read as Standards Australia
#ASSERT `the body a reference to the Standards Association of Australia is read as` FALSE EQUALS JUST "Standards Australia"
-- 74b. s 13B: the section does not reach a reference inside this Act
#ASSERT `the body a reference to the Standards Association of Australia is read as` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 75a. s 13C(a): irreversible cessation of all brain function is death
#ASSERT `the person has died` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 75b. s 13C(b): irreversible cessation of circulation of blood is death
#ASSERT `the person has died` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- 75c. s 13C: neither irreversible cessation: not death
#ASSERT `the person has died` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- 76. s 13D(1): a bankrupt under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 is "a bankrupt"
#ASSERT `the person is a bankrupt` (`Insolvency facts about a person` WITH `bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS TRUE, `a substantially similar status under a law applicable where that Act does not apply` IS FALSE, `a debtor party to a debt agreement under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS FALSE, `a debtor who has entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X and obligations remain to be discharged` IS FALSE, `not yet in a Part X agreement but has authorised a controlling trustee to perform functions under Part X` IS FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- 77a. s 13D(1): a debtor party to a debt agreement is not "a bankrupt"
#ASSERT `the person is a bankrupt` (`Insolvency facts about a person` WITH `bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS FALSE, `a substantially similar status under a law applicable where that Act does not apply` IS FALSE, `a debtor party to a debt agreement under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS TRUE, `a debtor who has entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X and obligations remain to be discharged` IS FALSE, `not yet in a Part X agreement but has authorised a controlling trustee to perform functions under Part X` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- 77b. s 13D(2)(b): a debtor party to a debt agreement is within "bankrupt or a person whose affairs are under insolvency laws"
#ASSERT `the person is a bankrupt or a person whose affairs are under insolvency laws` (`Insolvency facts about a person` WITH `bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS FALSE, `a substantially similar status under a law applicable where that Act does not apply` IS FALSE, `a debtor party to a debt agreement under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS TRUE, `a debtor who has entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X and obligations remain to be discharged` IS FALSE, `not yet in a Part X agreement but has authorised a controlling trustee to perform functions under Part X` IS FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- 78a. s 13D(2)(c): a Part X agreement with obligations remaining is within (2)
#ASSERT `the person is a bankrupt or a person whose affairs are under insolvency laws` (`Insolvency facts about a person` WITH `bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS FALSE, `a substantially similar status under a law applicable where that Act does not apply` IS FALSE, `a debtor party to a debt agreement under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS FALSE, `a debtor who has entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X and obligations remain to be discharged` IS TRUE, `not yet in a Part X agreement but has authorised a controlling trustee to perform functions under Part X` IS FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
-- 78b. s 13D(2)(c): a Part X agreement with all obligations discharged is not within (2)(c)
#ASSERT `the person is a bankrupt or a person whose affairs are under insolvency laws` (`Insolvency facts about a person` WITH `bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS FALSE, `a substantially similar status under a law applicable where that Act does not apply` IS FALSE, `a debtor party to a debt agreement under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS FALSE, `a debtor who has entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X and obligations remain to be discharged` IS FALSE, `not yet in a Part X agreement but has authorised a controlling trustee to perform functions under Part X` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- 79. s 13D(2)(d): a person who has authorised a controlling trustee but not yet entered the agreement is within (2)
#ASSERT `the person is a bankrupt or a person whose affairs are under insolvency laws` (`Insolvency facts about a person` WITH `bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS FALSE, `a substantially similar status under a law applicable where that Act does not apply` IS FALSE, `a debtor party to a debt agreement under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)` IS FALSE, `a debtor who has entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X and obligations remain to be discharged` IS FALSE, `not yet in a Part X agreement but has authorised a controlling trustee to perform functions under Part X` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
-- 80. s 14: "sections 5 to 8" covers 5 and 8 and what lies between
#ASSERT `the portions a reference covers` (LIST "s 5", "s 6", "s 7", "s 8", "s 9") "s 5" "s 8" EQUALS LIST "s 5", "s 6", "s 7", "s 8"
-- 81. s 15(1): "section 5" in an Act with nothing in the context to the contrary is section 5 of that Act
#ASSERT `an internal reference points at` `a Part, Chapter, section, schedule, appendix or form` FALSE EQUALS `the Act in which the reference is made`
-- 82. s 15(2): "paragraph (b)" in a provision is paragraph (b) of that provision
#ASSERT `an internal reference points at` `a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or other division of a provision` FALSE EQUALS `the provision in which the reference is made`
-- 83. s 15(3): "clause 3" in a schedule is clause 3 of that schedule
#ASSERT `an internal reference points at` `a clause, subclause, paragraph or other division in a schedule` FALSE EQUALS `the schedule, or the provision of the schedule, in which the reference is made`
-- 84a. s 15A: "paragraph" includes a subparagraph
#ASSERT `a reference to a paragraph includes` `a subparagraph` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 84b. s 15A: "paragraph" includes an item
#ASSERT `a reference to a paragraph includes` `an item` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 84c. s 15A(2): a reference to a paragraph includes the conjunction after it
#ASSERT `a reference to a paragraph includes the conjunction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 85. s 16(3): a reference to a Commonwealth Act is to that Act as amended from time to time
#ASSERT `the reference includes the law as it may from time to time be amended` `an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 86a. s 17: in a law passed in 1990, "or" is read disjunctively
#ASSERT `the word is read disjunctively and not as implying similarity` `the word or` (Date 1 1 1990) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 86b. s 17: where "similar" is added, the word is not read as ignoring similarity
#ASSERT `the word is read disjunctively and not as implying similarity` `the word or` (Date 1 1 1990) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 87. s 17: a law passed in 1970 is not reached by s 17
#ASSERT `the word is read disjunctively and not as implying similarity` `the word or` (Date 1 1 1970) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 88. s 18: the construction that promotes the purpose or object is preferred
#ASSERT `the construction preferred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the first construction`
-- 89. s 19(1)(a): outside material may be considered to confirm the ordinary meaning
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE `to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking account of its context and the purpose or object` EQUALS TRUE
-- 90a. s 19(1)(b)(i): outside material may be considered where the provision is ambiguous
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE `because the provision is ambiguous or obscure` EQUALS TRUE
-- 90b. s 19(1)(b)(ii): outside material may be considered where the ordinary meaning is manifestly absurd
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE `because the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` EQUALS TRUE
-- 91. s 19(1): where the ordinary meaning is clear and not absurd, outside material may not be used to find another meaning
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE `for some other reason` EQUALS FALSE
-- 92a. s 19(2)(e): an explanatory memorandum laid before the provision was enacted is within the list
#ASSERT `material of this kind is among the material that may be considered` `an explanatory memorandum, or other relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of either House by a Minister` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 92b. s 19(2)(e): one laid after the provision was enacted is not within the list
#ASSERT `material of this kind is among the material that may be considered` `an explanatory memorandum, or other relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of either House by a Minister` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 93. s 19(2)(f): the Minister's second reading speech is within the list
#ASSERT `material of this kind is among the material that may be considered` `the speech of a Minister moving the second reading of the Bill in a House` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 94a. s 19(2)(d): a treaty referred to in the written law is within the list
#ASSERT `material of this kind is among the material that may be considered` `a treaty or other international agreement referred to in the written law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 94b. s 19(2)(d): a treaty not referred to in the written law is not within the list
#ASSERT `material of this kind is among the material that may be considered` `material of some other kind` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 95. s 19(2)(b): a Law Reform Commission report laid before a House before enactment is within the list
#ASSERT `material of this kind is among the material that may be considered` `a report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body, laid before either House of Parliament` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 96. s 19(3): two matters are weighed (ordinary-meaning reliance; avoiding prolonged proceedings)
#ASSERT `ti count of strings` (`the matters regard must be had to when deciding whether to consider material, and what weight to give it`) EQUALS 2

-- ===================== PART III: COMMENCEMENT AND CITATION (ss 20-27) =====================

-- 97. s 20(1): Royal Assent 1984-06-15, no contrary intention: commences on the day of assent
#ASSERT `the day an Act comes into operation` `Royal Assent given` (Date 15 6 1984) NOTHING `nothing about it` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 1984)
-- 98. s 20(1): Royal Assent 1984-06-30 (the last day before 1 July 1984): commences on the day of assent
#ASSERT `the day an Act comes into operation` `Royal Assent given` (Date 30 6 1984) NOTHING `nothing about it` EQUALS JUST (Date 30 6 1984)
-- 99. s 20(1) displaced by s 2: this Act, assent 1984-05-31, names 1984-07-01
#ASSERT `the day an Act comes into operation` `Royal Assent given` (Date 31 5 1984) NOTHING (`a particular day` (Date 1 7 1984)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 1984)
-- 100. s 20(2): assent 1984-07-01: the 28th day after is 1984-07-29
#ASSERT `the day an Act comes into operation` `Royal Assent given` (Date 1 7 1984) NOTHING `nothing about it` EQUALS JUST (Date 29 7 1984)
-- 101. s 20(2): assent 2024-01-31: 2024-02-28
#ASSERT `the day an Act comes into operation` `Royal Assent given` (Date 31 1 2024) NOTHING `nothing about it` EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2024)
-- 102. s 20(2): assent 2024-02-05: 2024-03-04
#ASSERT `the day an Act comes into operation` `Royal Assent given` (Date 5 2 2024) NOTHING `nothing about it` EQUALS JUST (Date 4 3 2024)
